cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these materials, please cite this repository."
title: "Accessible Code-Generated Visualizations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kartali"
    given-names: "Aneta"
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/anjeta/accessible-code-generated-visualizations"
url: "https://ascnet.ie/access2cs/"
abstract: >
  Educational materials and reproducible examples for creating more accessible
  code-generated visualizations in Python and R, with particular attention to
  blind and visually impaired learners. The repository includes accessibility
  guidelines, graph examples, textual description workflows, and sonification
  examples developed in the context of the Erasmus+ Access2CS project.
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - data visualization
  - computer science education
  - Python
  - R
  - blind learners
  - visually impaired learners
  - Access2CS
